FILE 1: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts
Add near the other type aliases: `export type PivotAttempt = 1 | 2;`
EDIT A (function `seatEventId`): new signature `function seatEventId(pivotId: string, seatId: string, attempt: PivotAttempt = 1): string`. Attempt 1 returns exactly today's `${pivotId}:pivot_seat_returned:${seatId}`; attempt 2 returns `${pivotId}:attempt-2:pivot_seat_returned:${seatId}`.
EDIT B: add, directly below `seatEventId`, a helper
  function deliberationEventId(pivotId: string, attempt: PivotAttempt): string
returning `${pivotId}:pivot_deliberation_completed` for attempt 1 and `${pivotId}:attempt-2:pivot_deliberation_completed` for attempt 2. In `finalizePivotTransaction`, use it for the `eventId` of the `pivot_deliberation_completed` append.
EDIT C (exported function `buildPivotCouncilPaths`): add a third parameter `attempt: PivotAttempt = 1`; throw `new TypeError('attempt must be 1 or 2.')` when it is neither. Keep artifactRoot, pivotRoot, councilRoot, configPath, statePath and reportPath exactly as today. For attempt 1 keep seatsRoot, seatPaths and deliberationPath exactly as today. For attempt 2 use `const attemptRoot = join(councilRoot, 'attempt-2')`, `seatsRoot = join(attemptRoot, 'seats')`, seatPaths under that seatsRoot with the same three file names, and `deliberationPath = join(attemptRoot, 'deliberation.md')`.
EDIT D (interface `PersistedPivotConfig`): add `readonly attempt: PivotAttempt;` and change the invariants type to `{ readonly rounds: PivotAttempt; readonly seats: 3; readonly depth: 1; readonly recursionAllowed: false }`.
EDIT E (function `parsePersistedPivotConfig`): read `const attempt = value.attempt === undefined ? 1 : value.attempt;` and throw `new Error('Persisted pivot attempt must be 1 or 2.')` unless attempt is 1 or 2. Replace the `value.invariants.rounds !== 1` condition with `value.invariants.rounds !== attempt`. Return `attempt` and `invariants: { rounds: attempt, seats: 3, depth: 1, recursionAllowed: false }`. A config written before this change has no `attempt` key and `rounds: 1`, and must keep loading.
EDIT F (function `preparePivotTransaction`): the in-memory `configRecord` gets `attempt: 1` and `invariants.rounds: 1`, BUT the object passed to `persistConfig` must not carry an `attempt` key when attempt is 1, so configs stay byte-identical to today: build the persisted object as `const { attempt: _attempt, ...persistedRecord } = configRecord;` when attempt is 1, and pass `persistedRecord`. Also, when `resumed` is true, take `limits` from the persisted config (`readPersistedConfig(paths.configPath, pivotId).limits`) instead of `config`, so a pivot opened under older defaults resumes without a config conflict; use those same limits for the preflight. The pending result gets a new field `attempt: 1` (add `readonly attempt: PivotAttempt;` to `PivotPendingResult`). Seat-event lookups in prepare use `seatEventId(pivotId, seat.id, 1)`.
EDIT G (function `recordPivotSeatResult`): read `const attempt = persistedConfig.attempt;`, use `seatEventId(pivotId, seat.id, attempt)` for the event id, and add `...(attempt === 2 ? { attempt } : {})` to the event payload (attempt 1 events stay byte-identical).
EDIT H (function `finalizePivotTransaction`): read `const attempt = persistedConfig.attempt;` and look seat events up with `seatEventId(pivotId, seat.id, attempt)`.
Do NOT add any retry behavior; attempt 2 is only reachable from tests in this task.
